jose: My name is Josephine
jose: But I've always hated that name, It was too soft and too feminine

jose: Ever since I was a child, I felt different, i did not fit in and did not feel like the other girl's my age
jose: I felt like a guy trapped in a girl's body

jose: Ever since I was 5 I had refused to wear any sort of dress and my mom would cry saying I was a pretty girl and was being ungrateful
jose: But I did not feel pretty, I felt wrong

jose: When I was 7 I cut my hair short and my father yelled at me for doing that
jose: He said I looked like a boy and for once I felt...good

jose: When I was 9 I had began wearing male clothing but my parents did not like that
jose: I was punished and told to act like a lady, I was told to be...normal

jose: But I was never normal and would not want to ever be
jose: Then we moved to a new house and I met a girl named Mina

jose: She was small and shy but she looked at me like I was the most beautiful person she had ever seen
jose: And for the first time in my life...I felt accepted

jose: We quickly became friends. She never questioned my clothing nor behaviour
jose: She had simply accepted me for who I am

jose: I thought she understood me, I thought she saw me for who I was...But I was wrong
jose: As we grew up things began to change

jose: Mina had started to become possesive, she followed me everywhere and scared away anyone who had tried to get close to me
jose: She treated me like I was her's

jose: At first I thought it was sweet, I thought she was simply protecting me
jose: But then it became suffocating

n: Who were you talking to?
n: Why did'nt you wait for me?
n: You should not be friends with them?

jose: She was everywhere and I could'nt breath. It got so bad I began having panic attacks
jose: I could not sleep, could not eat. I felt like I was drowning

jose: And that's when my parents decided to send me to the hospital. Or rather the psychiatric ward
jose: I was diagnosed with gender dysphoria and anxiety

jose: Hoonestly...It was the best year of my life as for the first time I was surrounded by people who actually understood
jose: I learnt to accept myself, I learn that I was allowed to be who I wanted to be

jose: When I came back I was ready
jose: I told everyone that I wanted to be called Jose, that I wanted to be seen as male

jose: I cut my hair even shorter and I started binding
jose: And Mina...she smiled and accepted me

jose: But I knew by the look in her eyes that she hated it, she hated the person I was becoming
jose: She wanted to see the old me, The girl she fell in love with

jose: To me University was supposed to be a fresh start but Mina was still there
jose: She still followed me and try to remain possesive over me

jose: I felt trapped, I felt like I would never escape
jose: And then...I met Ruby

jose: We met on a dating app named Bu Xiang Ni which translated to Unlike You
jose: I found the name poetic

jose: Ruby was beautiful, he was soft and feminine, he wore dresses and makeup
jose: He was a femboy but he was so confident and unapologetically himself

jose: And he accepted me. He saw me as a man
jose: He held my hand and he kissed me and for the first time in my life again I felt free

jose: I had told him that I was born female but identified as male to everyone else
jose: And instead of eaving me that very moment he said...

ruby: I've known ever since the first day we had began talking and it does not matter to me
ruby: You are Josephine the person I fell in love with

jose: I cried so much that day because someone finally saw me and understood how I felt
jose: But I knew Mina would'nt understand and she would never accept Ruby

jose: So I hide it. But one day I could not hide it anymore
jose: I told her that I know had a girlfriend

jose: The look on her face was devastating, the look of betrayal and heartbreak
jose: And I felt guilty as I knew how much effort she put into loving me all this time

jose: But I knew she waw'nt in love with the real me but the stupid version of me she had in her head
jose: I could not stop I loved Ruby and needed Ruby as he was my escape

jose: At that moment I decided that Ruby and I will no longer e dating in secret but in public
jose: And I could see Mina watching us and following us and I had a gut feeling she was planning something

jose: I was extremely scared but I did not know what to do especially since Mina was my best friend
jose: She was the only person who had been with me for the longest time and I could'nt just abondon her

jose: But I should have....
jose: I should have ran, I should have protected Ruby from such an awful fate

jose: It happened at the park, both me and Ruby were sitting on a bench, kissing
jose: And all of a sudden all I could see was Ruby's body collapsing 

jose: I looked down and could see blood everywhere, I was horrified and when I turned to see who had done this I saw....
jose: MINA!!

jose: She had a knife and her eyes...her eyes were empty
jose: I asked her what she was doing

nn: I'm saving you and setting you free

jose: From what?

nn: From him and everyone in this world who wants to take me away from me

jose: I tried my best to run away but Mina was faster than me and was able to grab me, she held me close and I could feel her breath on my neck

nn: I've loved you for the past 15 years, You were mine...You were always mine

jose: Mina.... please... I was never yours

nn: I know and because of that I won't allow you to be with anyone else

jose: And then... I felt the knife go into my body and I fell to the ground
jose: As I lay dying I began to think about everything. My life, My identity and My love

jose: I thought about how I spent my whole life running from myself and from others who knew the truth and in the end.... I ran too late
jose: I thought about Mina my best friend, my protector and now my murderer

jose: I should have told her from the beginning about the truth that I was never the girl she loved and I was never hers
jose: But I was too scared

jose: And now....
jose: I would never get the chance

